{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/610966-a-host-of-gears-npc-thread","id":610966,"title":"A Host of Gears: NPC Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-01T09:56:02-07:00","id":610966,"title":"A Host of Gears: NPC Thread","content":"So, I figured &quot;why not make a place for people to share an ideas they've had for NPCs?&quot; Here's one to start;I'll try posting more later. Feel free to add your own!<br /> <br /> &quot;Chatterbox&quot;/&quot;Ami&quot;<br /> <br /> Story<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Mission</b><br /> The Angel known to local Unchained as &quot;Chatterbox&quot; exists to debrief those of the Machine's operatives that are not directly linked to its databases, such as cultists or humaniform Cryptids. <br /> <br /> <b>Description</b><br /> Operating out of a small convenience store near the edge of the city, the Angel rarely maintains the same appearance twice. What is consistent is that she appears to be a woman in her early twenties or late teens, usually conventionally attractive, wearing a name tag with &quot;Ami&quot;(she pronounces it &quot;Amy&quot;) written on it in a child-like script, the I dotted with a heart. She's always smiling, and tends towards an obnoxious level of cheer and enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> <b>Methods</b><br /> Her methods are rather simple. When others present to her the passcode, she ushers them into a small back room, where she uses her Numina and the building's Infrastructure to discern where the GM requires labor to be distributed, and then directs them on how to best contribute. <br /> <br /> Normally, her weakness and well-known location would have gotten her destroyed by now. However, she is considered to be far too much of a useful asset by many due to a unique flaw in her creation. She cannot understand the concepts of falsehood, description, and other concepts related to this. Anyone who gives the passcode will be debriefed, with no security measures or verification what so ever. This has made her very useful for those seeking to determine what and where the Machine's plans are.<br /> <br /> While the local Unchained expected her to be a threat, enough have risked the chance and come out relatively unscathed that they've come to the conclusion that she's a genuine glitch, proof that It is not as infallible as some would believe. Others have a different point of view. As far as they're concerned, Chatterbox is bait, the trigger for a massive trap just waiting for the outcasts to let down their guard. Even so, they've been hesitant to kill her; after all, that may just be what It wants...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Virtue: Helpful<br /> Vice: Innocent <br /> <br /> Rank: 1<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 4, Finesse 2, Resistance 2 <br /> <br /> Influence: Knowledge 1<br /> <br /> Corpus: 7<br /> Willpower: 4<br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Initiative: 4<br /> <br /> Numina: Voice of the Machine(As Embed), Hallucination, Omen Trance<br /> <br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form, Materialize, Discorporate <br /> <br /> Max Essence: 10<br /> <br /> Ban: Must always appear happy<br /> Bane: Bullets</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In general, the idea was inspired by the idea of a &quot;broken Angel&quot;, combined with the mention of the Unchained possibly having Servitor allies in the book. The idea is that she might serve as an unknowing quest giver, providing leads to Rings who have struck dry or don't have the time to search every nook and cranny for GM influence. And then, of course, is the chance she's 